-md text-nk-cold-brown-500 lg:col-span-3\",\"children\":[\"$L1f\",\"$L20\"]}],\"$L21\"]}]}],\"$L22\",\"$L23\"]}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26:I[80189,[\"2821\",\"static/chunks/2821-9b6ca5eba886e2a6.js\",\"5889\",\"static/chunks/5889-e987f21560aaf28e.js\",\"1356\",\"static/chunks/1356-5c8c2e2fb753b8c7.js\",\"2619\",\"static/chunks/2619-b8db57ac19da49ac.js\",\"8072\",\"static/chunks/8072-b586ce59c544e9ca.js\",\"5355\",\"static/chunks/5355-fe3e19517f6c5df1.js\",\"266\",\"static/chunks/266-dcbd378fe4c88330.js\",\"8018\",\"static/chunks/app/(main)/(webflow)/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-773edafb2f01b5ae.js\"],\"default\"]\n2c:I[13837,[\"2821\",\"static/chunks/2821-9b6ca5eba886e2a6.js\",\"5889\",\"static/chunks/5889-e987f21560aaf28e.js\",\"1356\",\"static/chunks/1356-5c8c2e2fb753b8c7.js\",\"2619\",\"static/chunks/2619-b8db57ac19da49ac.js\",\"8072\",\"static/chunks/8072-b586ce59c544e9ca.js\",\"5355\",\"static/chunks/5355-fe3e19517f6c5df1.js\",\"266\",\"static/chunks/266-dcbd378fe4c88330.js\",\"8018\",\"static/chunks/app/(main)/(webflow)/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-773edafb2f01b5ae.js\"],\"default\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1f:[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":\"38\",\"height\":\"9\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 38 9\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"role\":\"presentation\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M37.6667 4.5C37.6667 3.02724 36.4728 1.83333 35 1.83333C33.5272 1.83333 32.3333 3.02724 32.3333 4.5C32.3333 5.97276 33.5272 7.16667 35 7.16667C36.4728 7.16667 37.6667 5.97276 37.6667 4.5ZM0.646446 4.14644C0.451183 4.34171 0.451183 4.65829 0.646446 4.85355L3.82843 8.03553C4.02369 8.23079 4.34027 8.23079 4.53553 8.03553C4.7308 7.84027 4.7308 7.52369 4.53553 7.32842L1.70711 4.5L4.53553 1.67157C4.7308 1.47631 4.7308 1.15973 4.53553 0.964463C4.34027 0.769201 4.02369 0.769201 3.82843 0.964463L0.646446 4.14644ZM35 4.5L35 4L1 4L1 4.5L1 5L35 5L35 4.5Z\",\"fill\":\"#73695C\"}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"20:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Back to Longevity Articles\"}]\n24:T26f8,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eDo you ever feel older or younger than your driver's license age? Your chronological age, which is the number of birthdays you've had, is only part of the story. Your biological age represents your body's true condition at the cellular level, offering a more accurate picture of your health and longevity potential than your birth year.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhile biological age encompasses your entire body, your immune system plays a crucial role in determining your health trajectory. Immune age refers to the functional age of your immune system and predicts your healthspan, which is the years you will live in good health. An immune age test is a key step in preventive health, providing early insight into your body's ability to fight disease, resist infections, and maintain wellness.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003ca id=\"\" href=\"https://www.generationlab.com/the-systemage-test\"\u003eGeneration Lab's SystemAge test\u003c/a\u003e, a breakthrough that brings clinical-grade diagnostics to your home. This advanced at-home test measures your immune age alongside 18 other organ systems, empowering you to control your health before symptoms appear and optimize your biology for a longer, healthier life.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eWhat is Immune Age?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThink of it like a car. The model year is its age, but mileage and engine condition determine its performance. Your immune age is your engine's condition; it indicates your immune system's functioning regardless of your age. Two 50-year-olds can have different immune ages: one might have the immune function of a 35-year-old, while another might have the compromised immunity of a 65-year-old.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eAs we age, our immune system undergoes two processes that accelerate aging. Immunosenescence refers to the deterioration of the immune system, while inflammaging describes chronic, low-grade inflammation that drives aging. When your immune age exceeds your chronological age, these processes accelerate, increasing your risk for age-related diseases, infections, and cancer.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eUnderstanding your immune age is a critical health marker for several reasons:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003ePredicts Healthspan:\u003c/strong\u003e A younger immune age is linked to a longer healthy, active life free from chronic disease.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eEarly Disease Detection:\u003c/strong\u003e An elevated immune age can signal chronic conditions years before symptoms manifest.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eInfection Resilience:\u003c/strong\u003e Your first and strongest defense against viruses, bacteria, and other pathogens is a strong, youthful immune system.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eCancer Surveillance:\u003c/strong\u003e A well-functioning immune system is effective at identifying and eliminating pre-cancerous cells before they develop into tumors.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eHow Immune Age Testing Works\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eTraditional blood tests provide useful snapshots of your current health, but they don't measure the biological processes that drive aging at the cellular level. To understand your immune age, we need to look at epigenetics, which is the science of how your behaviors, environment, and lifestyle can cause changes that affect gene function without altering the DNA sequence.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe most accurate method for measuring biological age involves analyzing DNA methylation patterns throughout your genome. DNA methylation acts as a system of molecular switches that turn genes \"on\" or \"off.\" In a young, healthy body, these switches operate in organized, predictable patterns. As we age, these patterns become disorganized or \"noisy.\" This phenomenon, which is called biomolecular noise, is a hallmark of aging. Epigenetic age testing via DNA methylation analysis represents the gold standard for biological age measurement, pioneered by researchers at Harvard and UC Berkeley.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eAdvanced DNA methylation tests can analyze hundreds of thousands of methylation sites across your genome, creating a high-resolution picture of your molecular aging process. This technology enables us to move beyond simple biological age calculations to provide detailed, organ-specific aging analysis that gives you precise insight into how each system in your body is aging biologically.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eThe Best Immune Age Testing: SystemAge\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eGeneration Lab is a cutting-edge longevity science company co-founded by UC Berkeley professor Dr. Irina Conboy, known as the \"mother of longevity\" for her groundbreaking aging biology research. The SystemAge test represents over \u003ca id=\"\" href=\"https://www.generationlab.com/science\"\u003e20 years of Harvard and UC Berkeley research\u003c/a\u003e, bringing clinical-grade diagnostics with unprecedented precision to your home.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eYour Body's 19 Biological Ages\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge is the first and only test providing individual biological ages for 19 organ systems. This organ-specific aging analysis represents a revolutionary advancement in personalized health assessment. Knowing your overall biological age is helpful, but understanding that your heart might be aging faster than your brain, or that your immune system is functioning like someone 10 years younger, provides actionable intelligence for targeted interventions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eYour SystemAge report includes biological age analysis for these 19 critical systems:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eBrain Health \u0026amp; Cognition\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eImmune System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eReproductive System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eCardiac System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eInflammatory Regulation\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eMetabolism\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eTissue Regeneration\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eBlood Sugar \u0026amp; Insulin Control\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eHepatic System (Liver)\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eMuscular System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eSkeletal System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eNervous System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eRespiratory System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eDigestive System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eBlood \u0026amp; Vascular System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eUrinary System\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eOncogenesis (Cell Mutation)\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eFibrosis (Scar Tissue Formation)\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eAuditory System\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eClinical-Grade Accuracy, Validated by Science\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge delivers unprecedented precision through the analysis of 460+ DNA methylation biomarkers, achieving clinical-grade accuracy in detecting biological age changes. This has been validated across 2,000+ clinical test cases. The founding team's research includes 20+ peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals like \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eNature\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eAging\u003c/em\u003e, and \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eGeroScience\u003c/em\u003e, earning over 14,000 scientific citations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis precision and credibility is why SystemAge has earned the trust of over 150 longevity clinics worldwide and endorsements from leaders, including Harvard geneticist George Church. Choosing SystemAge gives you access to the same testing used in cutting-edge research institutions and premier longevity clinics.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eHow to Measure Immune Age at Home\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge makes sophisticated scientific testing accessible through a streamlined, user-friendly process:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eOrder Your Kit:\u003c/strong\u003e Your SystemAge test arrives securely at your doorstep with everything needed for sample collection.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eSimple, Needle-Free Sample:\u003c/strong\u003e Use the included blood collection device to provide a small sample from your upper arm. The process is completely needle-free and painless.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eMail It Back:\u003c/strong\u003e Place your sample in the provided pre-paid return mailer and drop it off at any mailbox or post office.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eGet Your Results:\u003c/strong\u003e Within 3-4 weeks, you'll receive your comprehensive digital report detailing your 19 biological ages through our secure online portal.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eWhy SystemAge is the Most Accurate Biological Age Test\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhen choosing a preventive health testing solution, precision and comprehensiveness determine the value you receive. Here's how SystemAge compares to other options:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge vs. TruDiagnostic:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge provides 19 organ system reports for complete health analysis with clinical-grade accuracy.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eTruDiagnostic offers fewer organ scores (~11 systems); like most epigenetic clocks, its clock uses Elastic Net regression, which selects CpG sites primarily to fit the training data, not because each is established as biologically meaningful.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge vs. Function Health:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge uses deep epigenetic analysis to detect \"biomolecular noise\" and predict health risks years before symptoms.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eFunction Health: Relies on 100+ standard blood biomarkers that reveal current health status but miss subtle epigenetic changes that predict future disease risk.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge vs. Tally Health:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge: Uses blood samples (the gold standard for DNA methylation analysis) backed by Dr. Conboy's 20+ years of pioneering aging research.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eTally Health: Uses cheek swab collection, which can be less reliable for systemic aging analysis despite notable scientific backing.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge is the only clinical-grade test that combines organ-specific analysis across 19 systems with clinical-grade accuracy. It enables personalized and measurable interventions for biological age reversal.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eConclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eYour age isn’t just an unchangeable number, it’s a dynamic biological process you can influence and optimize. The SystemAge immune age test provides the data and personalized action plan you need to transform aging from a passive process into one you can control and reverse.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eEvery day matters in your biological aging journey. The earlier you establish your baseline and begin targeted interventions, the more dramatic your potential improvements. Don't wait for symptoms or your next birthday to remind you that time is passing.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"21:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"lg:col-span-9 flex flex-col gap-10 lg:gap-[80px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-3 lg:gap-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"nk-heading-3 lg:nk-heading-2 text-nk-cold-brown-500\",\"children\":\"Immune Age Test: Determine Your Immune System's Age\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"nk-text-base text-nk-cold-brown-500\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2025-10-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"children\":\"October 15, 2025\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\" • \",\"By \",\"Alina Su\"]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-9 gap-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg whitespace-pre-line lg:col-span-6\",\"id\":\"gl_blog_content\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$24\"}}],\"$L25\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"27:T1882,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ch5 id=\"\"\u003e\u003cem id=\"\"\u003eAmong the top 1% of startup raises, the round will accelerate adoption of the SystemAge breakthrough aging diagnostic platform across 275+ clinics and tens of thousands of people worldwide\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/h5\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eSan Francisco, Calif., October 23, 2025\u003c/strong\u003e — \u003ca id=\"\" href=\"http://www.generationlab.com\"\u003eGeneration Lab\u003c/a\u003e, the company delivering breakthroughs in longevity science, today announced the completion of an $11 million seed funding round, bringing total funding to $15 million and placing the company in the top 1% of all startup seed raises. Led by Accel, the round also includes notable investors Samsung Next, Zone2, EDM legend Steve Aoki's Aoki Labs, NBA star Giannis Antetokounmpo's Build Your Legacy (BYL) Ventures, and actor Simu Liu's Markham Valley Ventures.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eLess than ten months post-launch, Generation Lab has achieved remarkable commercial traction with its SystemAge™ quantification of biological age—health of 19 organ systems/functions from intact primary blood results—that is based on discovery of the physiologic non-linear curve of DNA methylation aging. SystemAge greatly improves on alternatives that make predictions from man-made graphs after transforming data in a biologically arbitrary way. In less than a year of operation, the company has signed over 275 clinics worldwide, amassed more than 300 million human-aging data points, and achieved 99.9% diagnostic accuracy, providing for the first time a clinically relevant capacity for meaningful, well-controlled healthspan optimization—the next frontier in global and personalized medicine.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eMarket Leadership Through Clinical Adoption\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge™ has rapidly gained adoption across diverse healthcare settings, from leading academic medical centers to boutique wellness practices. The platform is trusted by renowned longevity physicians, professional athletes, and celebrities, with early advocates including leading longevity experts Professors David Sinclair and George Church of Harvard Medical School, Dr. Adeel Khan, award-winning author Dr. Michael Roizen, and Aubrey de Grey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\"We're witnessing a fundamental shift from reactive to proactive healthcare—led by consumers,\" said Alina Su, CEO and Co-founder of Generation Lab. \"Our explosive growth, from zero to 275+ clinic partners in under a year, demonstrates that both clinicians and consumers are hungry for actionable aging insights. This funding allows us to accelerate our mission of making longevity diagnostics the standard of care globally. We're not just measuring aging; we're creating the roadmap to reverse it.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\"Generation Lab is shaping the future of the longevity industry,\" said Kerry Wang, Partner at Accel. \"Alina, Michael, and Irina are building with conviction and credibility in a space that demands both. Their SystemAge™ platform combines solid science with strong commercial progress, creating a new category in data-driven healthcare. This is only the beginning.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eRevolutionary Science Driving Results\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge™ measures the progression of biological aging across 19 distinct physiological systems (cardiovascular, reproductive, immune, fibrotic, metabolic, regenerative, etc.), with comprehensive mechanistic insights that enable effective personalized intervention strategies. The platform's breakthrough dataset has already established striking causality between SystemAge-found biological dysregulation—noise and disease-propensity—later confirmed in clinical tests that would not have been otherwise prescribed to pre-symptomatic individuals. In contrast to subjective so-called biological clocks that make correlative predictions from biologically arbitrary numbers with decades-large errors, SystemAge objectively and accurately quantifies changes critical for health from intact primary data. Interestingly, 70% of tested individuals were found to be biologically older than their chronological age, and sadly, company founders age 1.5 times faster than investors.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\"What sets SystemAge™ apart is our systems-based approach to aging measurement using what we're calling 'biological noise,'\" explained Dr. Irina Conboy, Co-founder of Generation Lab and renowned aging researcher at UC Berkeley. \"While other platforms offer disease biomarkers, we've developed the first preventive health test detecting signals before symptoms appear. This is the most comprehensive aging diagnostic, analyzing how multiple organ systems age in concert. Our proprietary algorithms, trained on hundreds of millions of data points, don't just tell you how old you are—they reveal which specific systems are aging fastest and provide precise interventions to reverse the process.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eProven Clinical Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eReal-world clinical data demonstrates SystemAge™'s ability to guide effective interventions. Clinical studies of SystemAge before versus after MUSE Stemcell treatment have shown 13.6 years of brain age reversal and 4.9 years of reproductive system age reversal. Anti-inflammatory diets and targeted fasting protocols can measurably slow organ aging, while optimized exercise regimens can reverse heart and immune system biological age by multiple years within six months.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe platform is detecting aging signals before symptoms appear, enabling truly preventative care pathways that could transform healthcare economics and patient outcomes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eAbout Generation Lab\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eFounded by renowned aging researcher Dr. Irina Conboy, Generation Lab is pioneering the future of longevity diagnostics through its flagship SystemAge™ platform. The company's mission is to create the Ageless Generation by providing the most comprehensive, accurate, and actionable aging diagnostics available. Based in San Francisco, Generation Lab serves over 275 clinic partners worldwide. For more information, visit\u003ca id=\"\" href=\"http://www.generationlab.com\"\u003e www.generationlab.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e‍\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eMedia Contact:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAlex Plant\u003cbr\u003eGeneration Lab\u003cbr\u003ealex@generationlab.com\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e‍\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"28:T2fb7,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe connection between gut health and overall wellness is clearer than ever. Your gut microbiome serves as the foundation for countless health aspects, from energy levels and mood stability to immune function and longevity. As this understanding has grown, so has the demand for accessible ways to peek inside this complex ecosystem within us.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eEnter at-home gut health testing. Products like the Thorne Gut Health Test allow microbiome analysis from home, delivering personalized insights previously available only through expensive clinical testing. For health-conscious individuals seeking data-driven optimization, these \u003ca id=\"\" href=\"https://www.generationlab.com/the-systemage-test\"\u003etests unlock digestive system secrets\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eIn this review, we'll explore the critical question: Is the information revealed by Thorne gut health test reviews sufficient for longevity and disease prevention goals, while the tests reveal interesting microbial data? We'll examine what the Thorne test measures, analyze the user experience, and determine whether microbiome testing alone provides the insight needed for preventive health optimization.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eWhat is the Thorne Gut Health Test?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe Thorne Gut Health Test is a sophisticated consumer-grade microbiome analysis tool. Let's examine the science behind it and what users can expect from the testing process to understand its value and limitations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eThe Science Behind the Test: Metagenomic Sequencing\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe Thorne test uses metagenomic sequencing, a technology that creates a comprehensive census of all gut microorganisms. Unlike simpler tests that identify specific bacterial strains, metagenomic sequencing analyzes the complete genetic material of your entire microbial community, including bacteria, viruses, fungi, and archaea.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis whole-genome approach provides a detailed snapshot of your gut microbiome composition, offering insights into which microbes are present and their functional potential. The technology identifies genes that enable certain metabolic processes, indicating your gut's ability to produce beneficial compounds or process different nutrients.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eWhat's in the Box \u0026amp; The User Process\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe Thorne testing kit arrives with everything needed for sample collection: a sterile container, stabilizer fluid to preserve the sample during shipping, detailed instructions, and pre-paid return packaging. The process is straightforward and non-invasive. Users collect a small stool sample, mix it with the stabilizer, and ship it back to Thorne's laboratory using the provided materials.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eConvenience is significant. There are no doctor's visits, lab appointments, or scheduling issues. Sample collection to shipping takes under 10 minutes, making it accessible for busy professionals prioritizing their health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eThorne’s Measurement Promises\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe Thorne microbiome analysis provides key metrics and insights:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eGut Diversity Score\u003c/strong\u003e: A measure of microbial variety, with higher diversity linked to better health outcomes.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eDysbiosis Index\u003c/strong\u003e: An indicator of microbial imbalance suggesting digestive issues\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eProbiotic Levels\u003c/strong\u003e: Quantification of beneficial strains like Bifidobacterium and Lactobacillus\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003ePathogen Detection\u003c/strong\u003e: Identification of harmful microorganisms\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eSCFA Production Potential\u003c/strong\u003e: Analysis of your microbiome's ability to produce \u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eshort-chain fatty acids (SCFAs)\u003c/strong\u003e, crucial for gut barrier function.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eInflammation Markers\u003c/strong\u003e: Microbial signatures linked to inflammatory processes\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003ePersonalized Recommendations\u003c/strong\u003e: Customized dietary and supplement suggestions based on your unique microbial profile.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eAnalyzing the Thorne Results: What Do You Get?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhen your results arrive in 2-3 weeks, you get access to a digital dashboard that breaks down your microbial world into insights. The report combines visual elements such as charts showing bacterial abundance and diversity metrics, with written explanations that translate complex microbiome data into actionable information.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe centerpiece is your Gut Diversity Score, presented on a scale comparing your microbial variety to Thorne's reference population. This metric reflects that diverse ecosystems tend to be more resilient and stable. The Dysbiosis Index provides a single number indicating how far your microbiome deviates from optimal balance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe personalized recommendations section is appealing to users. The test suggests targeted dietary changes, lifestyle modifications, and supplement protocols based on your microbial composition. These recommendations often include specific Thorne products, but also provide general nutritional guidance independent of any brand.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003ePros: Accessibility and Basic Insights\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe Thorne test excels in making complex microbiology accessible to consumers. The at-home collection process eliminates barriers to exploring gut health, while the user-friendly report format makes scientific data comprehensible for non-experts.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe test offers a solid introduction to microbial diversity and beneficial bacteria for newcomers to gut health optimization. It serves as a starting point for understanding how diet and lifestyle choices influence the gut ecosystem, motivating positive health changes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eThe Cons: Snapshot Limitations\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eUser and expert reviews of the Thorne gut health test highlight significant limitations. The critical issue is temporal volatility because your microbiome composition can shift dramatically based on a single meal, a stressful day, poor sleep, or recent antibiotic use. The results represent one moment in time, potentially missing your microbiome's typical state.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe test reveals \u003cem id=\"\"\u003ewho\u003c/em\u003e is in your gut but provides limited insight into \u003cem id=\"\"\u003etheir actions\u003c/em\u003e or\u003cem id=\"\"\u003e your body’s response.\u003c/em\u003e Two people with similar microbial compositions might have different health outcomes based on factors the test can’t measure, such as gene expression, metabolic efficiency, or inflammation levels.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe recommendations remain generic, while somewhat personalized. Standard advice to \"increase fiber intake\" or \"consider probiotics\" does not account for your unique biology, genetics, or health goals beyond digestive optimization.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eIs Microbiome Data Enough for True Prevention?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis raises a pivotal question for health optimizers and biohackers: Does knowing your microbiome composition provide enough depth for meaningful longevity and disease prevention strategies, while it is interesting?\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe answer requires understanding the gut-organ axis, which is the communication between your digestive system and other organ systems. Your gut microbiome influences brain function (the gut-brain axis), liver metabolism (the gut-liver axis), immune responses, cardiovascular health, and bone density. Conversely, the health of these systems affects microbial composition and function.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe limitation of microbiome-only testing is that it cannot measure the \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eimpact\u003c/em\u003e of your gut on other organs or detect subtle, systemic changes that precede disease. It cannot reveal the \"biomolecular noise,\" which is the cellular-level dysfunction that accumulates before symptoms. Most critically for longevity-focused individuals, it cannot measure your biological age or track how your interventions affect your aging rate.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThink of a microbiome test as checking a train's passenger list. It's useful, but it doesn't indicate the engine's condition, track integrity, or schedule. For a comprehensive assessment, examine the infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eHow Epigenetics Reveals Your Body's True Story\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eEpigenetics is the next evolution in personalized health data. It’s the science of how your behaviors and environment change gene function. Unlike genetic testing that reveals your DNA sequence, epigenetics shows how your genes function in response to your lifestyle choices.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe primary mechanism is DNA methylation. These are tiny biological markers that attach to your DNA, acting like volume controls for your genes. These patterns change throughout your life based on diet, exercise, stress, sleep, and environmental exposures. They represent your body's molecular memory of your lifestyle and its effects on cellular health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eAs we age, DNA methylation patterns become disorganized, creating \"biomolecular noise,\" a driver of aging and chronic disease development. Remarkably, epigenetic changes that signal disease risk are detectable years or sometimes decades before symptoms appear, providing an opportunity for preventive intervention.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis represents the \"why\" that microbiome testing misses. While gut tests analyze the external inhabitants of your digestive system, epigenetic testing analyzes your body's internal operating system at the cellular level, measuring the long-term impact of your lifestyle choices on your biological age and disease risk.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe premier tool for measuring these critical epigenetic patterns is Generation Lab's SystemAge test, which offers insights that make microbiome data a single chapter in a larger health story.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge: GPS for Your Health vs. Gut Snapshot\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eFor individuals serious about longevity and preventive health, SystemAge functions as a GPS for your biological journey. It provides precise coordinates for your current state, future path, and optimal destination. This isn't just marketing; it's grounded in 20 years of research at UC Berkeley and Harvard. It was co-founded by renowned UC Berkeley professor Dr. Irina Conboy, the \"mother of longevity research.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe key differentiator is SystemAge's ability to provide 19 distinct biological ages, one for each major organ system. This health map allows you to identify which systems are aging faster and target interventions precisely. You may discover that while your cardiovascular system is healthy, your immune system is aging rapidly, requiring specific lifestyle adjustments you wouldn't consider based on gut bacteria alone.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis organ-specific insight explains why some people see dramatic results from certain interventions while others see little benefit. Their biological aging patterns are unique, requiring personalized strategies that only comprehensive epigenetic analysis can reveal.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eConclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eOur analysis reveals that \u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne gut health test reviews\u003c/strong\u003e show it serves as a decent entry-level tool for individuals curious about their microbiome. It provides accessible insights into an important wellness aspect and can motivate positive dietary changes for those beginning their health optimization journey.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eHowever, when viewed through the lens of serious longevity and disease prevention goals, the test's limitations become apparent. As a volatile snapshot lacking the depth to guide comprehensive health strategies, microbiome testing alone falls short of providing the actionable intelligence needed for meaningful biological control.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eEpigenetic testing represents the gold standard for health-conscious individuals ready to move beyond basic insights and master their biological aging process. While gut testing tells you about one ecosystem in your body, epigenetic analysis reveals how your entire biological system responds to your lifestyle choices at the cellular level.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe choice comes down to your goals: Are you seeking information about your gut bacteria, or are you committed to slowing your biological age and potentially reversing it? Don't just manage your gut; master your biology. Turn aging into a measurable game.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"29:T2fbc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhat if your driver's license and your body's internal clock told different stories? For most of us, they do. You might be 45 according to your birth certificate, but your cells could be aging like someone much older or younger. The difference between your chronological age (the birthday number) and your biological age (your body's true, cellular age) is an important health metric you're not tracking.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eChronological age is a poor predictor of health and longevity. Two people born on the same day can have vastly different disease risks, energy levels, and lifespans. The key to understanding your health trajectory lies in measuring your biological age, which reflects how your lifestyle, genetics, and environment have impacted your body at the cellular level.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe good news? Biological age isn't just a concept; it's measurable, trackable, and modifiable. This guide will walk you through methods to check biological age, from basic biomarker panels to the gold standard of preventive health testing. By the end, you'll understand how to control your healthspan and turn aging into a game you can win.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eWhat Biological Age Is\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThink of biological age as the body's \"odometer,\" not just the \"model year.\" While chronological age counts the years since birth, biological age measures the functioning of your cells and organs compared to the average population. It's the difference between asking \"How long has this car been on the road?\" versus \"How many miles has it traveled and how well is the engine running?\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis distinction matters more than you realize. Your biological age correlates with real-world outcomes that impact your daily life. These outcomes include your risk of chronic diseases like heart disease and diabetes, your energy levels, cognitive function, and overall healthspan, which is the years you'll live in good health. Someone with a younger biological age than their chronological age typically enjoys better health, more vitality, and a lower risk of age-related diseases. Conversely, accelerated biological aging can signal increased disease risk years before symptoms appear.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe science behind biological aging centers on epigenetics and DNA methylation. Tiny \"dimmer switches\" on your DNA control gene expression. Over time, due to lifestyle factors, stress, and environmental exposures, some switches malfunction, creating \"noise\" in your genetic instructions. A DNA methylation test measures this noise, providing a precise picture of your cells' molecular aging.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eKey takeaways about biological age:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eIt reflects your true cellular health and aging rate.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eIt can differ significantly from your chronological age.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eTargeted interventions can influence and reverse it.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003e4 Ways to Check Your Biological Age\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eMethods to measure biological aging vary in accuracy, scope, and actionability. Some provide basic health snapshots, while others offer deep insights into aging trajectory and disease risk. Let's break down the top four methods, from basic to advanced.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eMethod 1: Standard Blood Biomarker Panels\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eStandard blood biomarker panels measure 100+ common markers in your blood, including cholesterol, glucose, liver enzymes, inflammatory markers, and vitamin levels. Companies like Function Health have popularized this approach, offering comprehensive panels that provide a broad snapshot of your current physiological state.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eBiomarker panels appeal due to their accessibility and familiarity. Most people understand cholesterol and blood sugar concepts, and these tests reveal important information about cardiovascular health, metabolic function, and nutritional status. They're also affordable and widely available through traditional healthcare and direct-to-consumer companies.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eBiomarker panels have significant limitations in measuring biological age. They are reactive, reflecting recent activity, such as what you ate last week, how you slept last night, or whether you exercised yesterday, rather than long-term aging patterns. A single high glucose reading might indicate a large meal before testing, not a rapidly aging metabolic system. These tests lack the epigenetic depth needed to detect the subtle \"biomolecular noise\" signaling disease risk years in advance. They measure the consequences of aging rather than the aging process.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eMethod 2: Telomere Length Testing\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eTelomere testing has gained popularity in longevity circles due to its intuitive concept. Telomeres are protective DNA-protein structures that cap chromosome ends, compared to shoelace tips. Each cell division shortens telomeres, leading to the theory that telomere length serves as a cellular \"aging clock.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe concept is easy to understand and has been extensively studied. Research links shorter telomeres to increased mortality risk and age-related diseases. Several direct-to-consumer companies offer telomere testing, marketing it as a way to measure biological age.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eHowever, science has evolved, and telomere length is a poor predictor of mortality or health compared to advanced methods. It's variable between individuals and can fluctuate based on temporary factors like stress or illness. More critically, it provides a single data point that often misrepresents overall health. Your telomeres might suggest one thing about your biological age while your cardiovascular, immune, and neurological systems tell different stories. It's like assessing a car's condition by looking only at the tires.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eMethod 3: Glycan Analysis\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eGlycan analysis represents a more sophisticated approach, focusing on glycans, which are complex sugars that modify proteins and play crucial roles in cellular communication and immune function. Companies like GlycanAge measure these sugar modifications to assess systemic inflammation and immune system aging, providing an \"immune age.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis method offers valuable insights into one aspect of aging: chronic inflammation, or \"inflammaging.\" Since inflammation drives many age-related diseases, understanding your immune system's aging pattern can help with health optimization.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe limitation of glycan analysis is its narrow focus. While knowing your \"immune age\" is useful, it tells you nothing about the aging of your brain, heart, metabolic system, or other crucial organs. It's like having a detailed report on one room of your house while being in the dark about the foundation, electrical system, and structural integrity. For a complete picture of your biological aging, you need comprehensive analysis across multiple organ systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eMethod 4: Advanced Epigenetic Testing\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe most accurate and validated method to check biological age is advanced epigenetic age testing via DNA methylation. This approach, developed over two decades at UC Berkeley and Harvard, measures the cumulative effects of time, lifestyle, and environment on gene expression. This is the definition of biological aging.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eUnlike other methods that look at downstream consequences of aging, epigenetic testing examines the mechanisms that control gene regulation. DNA methylation patterns are stable and predictive, providing consistent insights regardless of recent sleep or stress. This technology has been validated in thousands of studies and published in prestigious journals like Nature, Aging, and GeroScience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe most advanced epigenetic tests can move beyond single-number biological age calculations. The best platforms analyze aging patterns across your body, measuring organ-specific aging. Instead of learning you're biologically \"38 years old,\" you might discover your cardiovascular system is aging like a 35-year-old while your metabolic system shows patterns of a 42-year-old. This insight enables targeted interventions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis technology represents the pinnacle of longevity science. One company has perfected this approach, co-founded by the \"mother of longevity.\" The company brings clinical-grade diagnostics from the world's top research labs directly to consumers who want to control their health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eBest Biological Age Test\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge is a breakthrough in biological age testing. It is the first and only at-home test that delivers clinical-grade, organ-specific aging analysis directly to consumers. SystemAge was developed from 20 years of research at UC Berkeley by Dr. Irina Conboy, a pioneer in aging research. It transforms our understanding and management of aging.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eUnmatched Precision \u0026amp; Personalization:\u003c/strong\u003e Unlike tests that provide a single biological age, SystemAge delivers 19 distinct biological ages across your body's major organ systems. You'll discover the individual aging patterns of your Cardiovascular System, Brain Health \u0026amp; Cognition, Immune System, Metabolism, Liver Function, Kidney Health, and more. This analysis reveals that aging isn't uniform. Different body parts age at different rates.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eUnrivaled Early Detection:\u003c/strong\u003e SystemAge functions as a \"DNA methylation noise detector,\" identifying molecular signals of aging and disease risk years before symptoms. This early warning system enables proactive interventions when they are most effective, embodying the principle of prevention over treatment.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eActionable Intelligence:\u003c/strong\u003e Every SystemAge report transforms complex epigenetic data into a clear, personalized optimization roadmap. You receive science-backed intervention plans tailored to each organ system's needs, turning insights into action.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eMeasurable Results:\u003c/strong\u003e SystemAge lets you track your biological age reversal in real-time. Users following personalized recommendations have documented reductions of 5.5 to 13.6 years, proving aging can be measured, managed, and modified.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eHow to Measure Your Biological Age at Home\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge is designed to be simple, convenient, and stress-free for measuring your biological age at home:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eOrder Your Kit Online:\u003c/strong\u003e Your SystemAge test kit, which includes everything you need for sample collection, is delivered to your door.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eCollect Your Sample:\u003c/strong\u003e Use the innovative, needle-free blood collection device to gather your sample in minutes. No painful finger pricks or clinic visits are required.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eMail It Back:\u003c/strong\u003e Place your sample in the included pre-paid mailer and drop it in any mailbox. Your sample is securely transported to Generation Lab's advanced laboratory.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eGet Your Results:\u003c/strong\u003e Within 3-4 weeks, receive your comprehensive digital report detailing your 19 organ-specific biological ages and personalized optimization action plans.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe process takes under 10 minutes and offers insights that can transform your health and longevity approach.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eConclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eChronological age is outdated. It is a simple number that reveals nothing about your body's true condition or health trajectory. The future of health lies in understanding, tracking, and improving your biological age across all your body's systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThink of SystemAge as GPS for your health journey. Just as GPS provides turn-by-turn directions to reach your destination, SystemAge reveals your current biological age and the roadmap to optimize each organ system. This is empowerment through knowledge. It is the ability to make data-driven decisions about your health rather than hoping for the best.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eResearch shows biological age is modifiable. Users who achieved 5.5 to 13.6-year reductions in their biological age relied on precise, organ-specific data to guide their interventions, tracked their progress, and proved aging is not an inevitable decline but a manageable process.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e‍\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:T297c,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe gut-brain axis. The microbiome revolution. The realization that your digestive system influences everything from immune function to mental clarity has transformed our health perspective. With this awakening comes an explosion of at-home testing options promising personalized insights that could change your life.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eTwo names top every \"best gut health test\" list: Thorne and Viome. Both offer sophisticated microbiome analysis but use different approaches. For health-conscious consumers trying to optimize their well-being, the Thorne vs. Viome decision can feel overwhelming. Which test provides the most valuable insights for your health goals?\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eBut here's a deeper question that may reshape your gut health testing perspective: Is analyzing your diet and stool the full story? Or is there a more fundamental way to \u003ca id=\"\" href=\"https://www.generationlab.com/the-systemage-test\"\u003emeasure the health of your digestive system\u003c/a\u003e and your entire body at the cellular level? In this gut health test comparison, we'll explore not just which test wins, but whether there's a more powerful approach to understanding your health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eThorne vs Viome: What Are You Testing?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eBefore discussing features and costs, it's crucial to understand what these tests measure. Thorne and Viome analyze genetic material from microorganisms in your stool sample, but they look at different aspects of your microbial ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThorne's approach uses shotgun metagenomics, which is a method that identifies \u003cem id=\"\"\u003egut\u003c/em\u003e microbial species and maps their genetic potential. It conducts a detailed census of your gut community, revealing who lives there, the diversity of your microbial neighborhood, and their capabilities based on their genetics. This provides an overview of your microbiome's composition and balance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eViome uses metatranscriptomics, which is technology that identifies \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eactive\u003c/em\u003e and expressed microbial genes. If metagenomics is the census, metatranscriptomics is recording the town hall meeting. It reveals who lives in your gut and what they're doing in real-time. This approach focuses on current microbial activity and the biochemical pathways influencing your health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eBoth technologies offer valuable and distinct perspectives on the same biological system, one structural and one functional.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eThorne vs. Viome: A Feature Breakdown\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eLet's examine the core features of Thorne and Viome side-by-side to decide between them. We will compare the science, sample collection, final reports, and pricing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eCore Technology:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne Gut Health Test:\u003c/strong\u003e Utilizes Shotgun Metagenomic Sequencing, which identifies microbial DNA to understand your gut's potential.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eViome Gut Intelligence Test:\u003c/strong\u003e Employs Metatranscriptomic Sequencing, identifying active microbial RNA to focus on your gut’s activity.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhat It Measures:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne:\u003c/strong\u003e Measures microbial species, gut diversity, key pathways, and provides a gut dysbiosis score.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eViome:\u003c/strong\u003e Measures active microbial functions, metabolic pathways, and how your body metabolizes food and supplements.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSample Collection:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eBoth Thorne and Viome require an at-home stool sample.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eKey Report Insights:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne:\u003c/strong\u003e Offers scores for inflammation, diversity, pathogen presence, and nutrient production. Provides personalized diet, supplement, and lifestyle recommendations.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eViome:\u003c/strong\u003e Delivers scores for over 20 gut and microbial pathways, personalized food recommendations (Enjoy, Minimize, Avoid), and precision supplement formulas.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eScientific Backing:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne:\u003c/strong\u003e Relies on established metagenomic analysis methods.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eViome:\u003c/strong\u003e Emphasizes its proprietary AI engine (VIE) and a focus on gene expression.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eTurnaround Time:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne:\u003c/strong\u003e Typically takes 5-6 weeks.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eViome:\u003c/strong\u003e Generally takes 2-3 weeks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eCost:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eThorne:\u003c/strong\u003e A one-time purchase of $399.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eViome:\u003c/strong\u003e Ranges from $199-$299, with subscription options available.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eIf you're the \"Who Lives There\" person\u003c/strong\u003e, Thorne excels at providing a detailed blueprint of your gut's microbial composition. This approach is ideal for understanding the foundational architecture of your gut ecosystem. It's a structural analysis for understanding diversity, identifying imbalances, and getting a comprehensive view of your microbiome's genetic capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eIf you're the \"What Are They Doing\" person\u003c/strong\u003e, Viome shines by focusing on current microbial activity and function. Its recommendations tie directly to the biochemical processes in your gut. This real-time functional analysis is perfect for someone wanting actionable insights based on what their microbes are producing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eBoth approaches share a fundamental limitation: they analyze the \u003cem id=\"\"\u003einhabitants\u003c/em\u003e of your gut ecosystem, not measure the health and biological age of the \u003cem id=\"\"\u003ehouse\u003c/em\u003e itself, your digestive system's cells and tissues.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eBeyond the Microbiome to Your Biological Age\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eYou've analyzed your gut's microbial inhabitants with Thorne or Viome. You've implemented their dietary recommendations and taken their suggested supplements. But here's the critical question: How do you know if these changes are impacting your health at the fundamental level, which is the aging and function of your digestive system's cells?\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eYour gut health influences and is influenced by your body's core aging processes through a master control system called epigenetics. While your DNA sequence remains constant, epigenetic mechanisms, particularly DNA methylation, act like molecular switches that turn genes on and off throughout your life. These switches control how your cells age, function, and respond to disease. Epigenetics is the GPS for your health: while your microbiome represents one road, your epigenetics is the entire navigation system, showing the condition of every highway and pathway in your body.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003e\u003ca id=\"\" href=\"https://www.generationlab.com/the-systemage-test\"\u003eGeneration Lab's SystemAge test\u003c/a\u003e represents a revolutionary leap in personalized health assessment. It's a clinical-grade epigenetic testing solution that measures your biological age across 19 organ systems, including your Digestive System. Co-founded by UC Berkeley's Dr. Irina Conboy, the \"mother of longevity,\" SystemAge is backed by over 20 years of research in cellular aging and regeneration.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eInstead of analyzing microbial activity, SystemAge measures the \"DNA methylation noise\" in your digestive system's cells. This detects molecular signatures of aging and disease risk years before symptoms. This provides a true biological age for your digestive system, offering insight into how your gut health strategies impact your cellular health and longevity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge vs Thorne vs Viome\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eA gut microbiome test provides a snapshot of one biological system, while SystemAge delivers a panoramic view of your body's aging process. It's the only at-home test that moves beyond aggregate scores to provide organ-level resolution, enabling targeted interventions based on where you're aging fastest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge Advantage:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eOrgan-Level Precision\u003c/strong\u003e: You receive 19 individual biological ages for systems like your Digestive, Immune, Brain Health, Cardiac System, and more, instead of one biological age number. This pinpoints \u003cem id=\"\"\u003ewhere\u003c/em\u003e you are aging fastest and need attention.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eClinical-Grade Accuracy\u003c/strong\u003e: SystemAge boasts clinical-grade accuracy in detecting biological age changes. This accuracy has been validated across 2,000+ test cases and published in top-tier peer-reviewed journals like \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eNature\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eAging\u003c/em\u003e. This precision far exceeds other consumer health tests.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eEarly Detection Power\u003c/strong\u003e: It's the only test that detects \"biomolecular noise\", subtle epigenetic changes that signal disease risk and organ dysfunction years before symptoms emerge. This is true preventive medicine, catching problems at the cellular level.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eActionable, Personalized Plans\u003c/strong\u003e: Your results include personalized intervention strategies for each organ system. If your Digestive System shows accelerated aging, your plan will target gut-specific interventions instead of generic recommendations.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003e\u003cstrong id=\"\"\u003eTrack Your Progress\u003c/strong\u003e: SystemAge is the ultimate biohacking tool to measure, intervene, and retest to verify your health strategies’ impact. Documented case studies show proven reductions in biological age of 5.5 to 13.6 years.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge provides the highest resolution map of your body's aging process available to consumers, and it is trusted by 150 longevity clinics worldwide.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eConclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eIn the Thorne vs. Viome comparison, both tests offer valuable but limited perspectives. Thorne provides a structural census of your microbial community, while Viome delivers a functional activity report of your microbes. Both are tools for understanding your gut microbiome's composition and activity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eIf your goal extends beyond managing your gut microbiome to controlling your biological aging process, the choice is clear. You need the highest resolution health map available that measures the inhabitants of your body's systems and the health and aging rate of the systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge represents the next evolution in personalized, preventive healthcare. Instead of guessing if your health strategies are working, measure what matters: your biological age across all major organ systems. Don't just manage your gut health; master your entire aging process with unprecedented precision and scientific rigor. Turn aging into a game you can win by understanding your body at the cellular level.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:T27bc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhat if your driver's license only told half your age? Your chronological age, the number of candles on your cake, is only half the story. Science shows a more important number: your biological age. While chronological age ticks forward each year, biological age reflects how well your cells, tissues, and organs are functioning. This number tells the real story of your health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eHere's the truth: biological age isn't fixed. It can be influenced, slowed, and even reversed. Age reversal isn't science fiction, it's due to understanding cellular mechanisms like epigenetics, the molecular switches that control gene expression. Advances in DNA methylation research show the aging process is more malleable than we imagined.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWith countless \"anti-aging\" products and fads flooding the wellness industry, how do you know what works? This guide delivers seven strategies grounded in robust scientific research. It reveals a critical truth: effective age reversal requires not just action, but precise measurement. You can't manage what you don't measure.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003e7 Science-Backed Age Reversal\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #1: Adopt an Anti-Inflammatory, Nutrient-Dense Diet\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eChronic inflammation accelerates aging, driving cellular damage through \"inflammaging.\" Research in \u003cem id=\"\"\u003eNature\u003c/em\u003e shows diets rich in polyphenols and omega-3 fatty acids, such as the Mediterranean diet, combat inflammation at the epigenetic level by influencing DNA methylation. These anti-inflammatory compounds reprogram genetic expression toward a younger biological state.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eImplementation Steps:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eBuild your plate around colorful plants, healthy fats (olive oil, avocados, nuts), and lean protein like wild-caught fish.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eDrastically reduce processed foods, added sugars, and industrial seed oils, which are pro-inflammatory drivers.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eIncorporate polyphenol-rich foods like berries, green tea, and dark leafy greens daily.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis nutritional approach impacts your Digestive, Cardiac, Inflammation Regulation, and Blood Sugar \u0026amp; Insulin Control biological ages and often shows improvements within 8-12 weeks of consistent implementation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #2: Integrate Smart, Consistent Exercise\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe right exercise prescription acts like a master key for age reversal. A combination of High-Intensity Interval Training (HIIT) and resistance training improves cardiovascular efficiency, boosts muscle protein synthesis, and promotes cellular cleanup through autophagy. Harvard research shows this exercise combination can improve mitochondrial function, which are the powerhouses of your cells, by up to 69% in older adults.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eHow to Implement It:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eAim for 2-3 HIIT sessions per week, focusing on total workouts of 20 minutes (including warm-up and cool-down).\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eIncorporate 2-3 days of strength training, emphasizing major muscle groups with progressive overload.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eAdd daily movement like walking to support recovery and maintain metabolic health.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThis exercise protocol benefits your Muscular, Skeletal, Cardiac Systems, and Metabolism biological ages. Many clients see 3-7 year improvements in these systems within six months of consistent training.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #3: Prioritize Deep, Restorative Sleep\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSleep is when your body does its critical age-reversal work. During deep sleep, your brain's glymphatic system activates, clearing toxic proteins associated with neurodegeneration. Growth hormone surges during sleep, promoting cellular repair, while poor sleep accelerates epigenetic aging across organ systems. Studies show people who get 7-9 hours of quality sleep have biological ages 1-2 years younger than poor sleepers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eImplementation Steps:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eMaintain a strict sleep schedule by going to bed and waking up at the same time, even on weekends.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eCreate an optimal sleep environment that is cool (65-68°F), completely dark, and quiet.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eImplement a digital sunset by avoiding screens for at least one hour before bed.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eQuality sleep is crucial for your Brain Health \u0026amp; Cognition, Neurodegeneration, and Immune System biological ages. Sleep optimization shows the fastest measurable improvements in biological age testing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #4: Manage Your Stress\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eChronic stress accelerates biological aging by elevating cortisol levels that drive systemic inflammation and epigenetic aging across organs. Conversely, stress-reduction practices like meditation lower inflammatory markers and lengthen telomeres, which are the protective caps on chromosomes. A study found regular meditators had biological ages 7-12 years younger than non-meditators.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eImplementation Steps:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003ePractice daily mindfulness meditation or breathwork for 10-15 minutes.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eSpend time in nature regularly to reduce cortisol levels.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eDevelop stress-interruption techniques like box breathing (4-4-4-4 pattern) for acute stress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eStress management affects nearly all biological systems and shows pronounced effects on Inflammation Regulation, Immune System, and Brain Health \u0026amp; Cognition ages.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #5: Consider Targeted Supplementation (with a Caveat)\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eWhile a food-first approach is optimal, certain supplements have robust research supporting their role in cellular health and age reversal. High-quality Omega-3s, Vitamin D3, and NAD+ precursors like NMN impact biological aging markers. However, supplementation without testing is ineffective because your body’s needs differ from generic recommendations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eImplementation Steps:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eBefore supplementing, get comprehensive bloodwork to identify nutrient deficiencies.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eChoose high-bioavailability forms from reputable brands that are third-party tested.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eStart with one supplement at a time to assess its impact.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eEffects vary by supplement, but they can significantly influence your Immune System (Vitamin D), Brain Health (Omega-3s), and Metabolism (NAD+ precursors) biological ages.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #6: Cultivate Strong Social Connections\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSocial isolation carries the same mortality risk as smoking 15 cigarettes daily. Strong social bonds reduce inflammation and improve health outcomes across all ages. Research shows people with robust social connections have lower inflammatory markers and better epigenetic expression. The biological impact of loneliness accelerates cellular aging.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eImplementation Steps:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col id=\"\"\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eSchedule regular, meaningful time with friends and family.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eJoin clubs or groups focused on hobbies or interests you are passionate about.\u003c/li\u003e  \u003cli id=\"\"\u003eVolunteer in your community to create purpose-driven connections.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eStrong social bonds affect biological aging by reducing chronic stress that accelerates aging in your Inflammation Regulation and Immune System networks.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"\"\u003eStrategy #7: Explore Cutting-Edge Therapies\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eFor those ready to explore age reversal, advanced interventions are showing remarkable results. Therapeutic plasma exchange (TPE), based on research by Generation Lab co-founder Dr. Irina Conboy, has documented cases showing a 10.4-year reduction in immune system age. Emerging therapies like targeted stem cell treatments have shown average reductions of 5.5 years in biological age. These are not experimental treatments, they're backed by rigorous clinical research.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThese advanced protocols should be explored with qualified practitioners in clinical settings. Research clinics offering these services and ensure they use proper biological age testing to track efficacy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eAdvanced therapies can profoundly affect systems like your Immune System, Tissue Regeneration, and Blood \u0026amp; Vascular System. Cases show a 13.6-year reduction in brain biological age.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eThe First Step to Reversing Your Age: Get Your Baseline\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eYou can't manage what you don't measure. Starting a new diet or exercise routine without a baseline is like driving without a map. You might feel like you're moving, but you don't know if you're heading in the right direction. To optimize your biology and achieve measurable age reversal, you need to know your starting point. Consider it your GPS for health.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eThe gold standard for measuring biological age is DNA methylation analysis, which are the epigenetic \"dimmer switches\" on genes controlling their function. Generation Lab's SystemAge test analyzes over 460 DNA methylation biomarkers to provide the most comprehensive picture of biological age. This clinical-grade epigenetic testing, founded by \u003ca id=\"\" href=\"https://www.generationlab.com/about\"\u003eDr. Irina Conboy\u003c/a\u003e, a renowned UC Berkeley scientist with over 20 years of longevity research, represents the cutting edge of age measurement science.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eSystemAge surpasses any other market test. It acts as a DNA methylation noise detector to give the biological age of 19 organ systems, including the Cardiac System, Brain Health \u0026amp; Cognition, Immune System, Metabolism, Muscular System, and 14 others, instead of a single \"biological age.\" This analysis allows you to target your interventions precisely.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"\"\u003eConclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eStrategic, science-backed interventions can achieve age reversal. The strategies are only as effective as your ability to measure their impact. Aging is not a fixed destiny but a dynamic process you can influence and control. With the right data and targeted approach, you can turn aging into a game you can win.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp id=\"\"\u003eDon't wait for symptoms or \"someday\" to take control of your biological destiny. Every day without baseline data is a missed opportunity for optimization. Your journey to a younger, healthier you starts with a simple step: knowing your numbers.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"22:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full bg-nk-beige-300 pt-8 pb-[60px] lg:pt-[60px] lg:pb-[100px] overflow-hidden relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"blogList\":[{\"id\":\"68f9ea1be2c945e8a979030e\",\"cmsLocaleId\":\"66abe8ff91c980538e9fe16c\",\"lastPublished\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:35.439Z\",\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:35.439Z\",\"createdOn\":\"2025-10-23T08:40:59.793Z\",\"isArchived\":false,\"isDraft\":false,\"fieldData\":{\"post-body\":\"$27\",\"post-summary\":\"Generation Lab, the company delivering breakthroughs in longevity science, today announced the completion of an $11 million seed funding round, bringing total funding to $15 million and placing the company in the top 1% of all sta\",\"main-image\":{\"fileId\":\"698d1edb954be89e2819ece9\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1edb954be89e2819ece9_68fa4901ee04a97a9885dd07_2a8da5d824cb3cf7cd93fc7d585d93b3.webp\",\"alt\":null},\"category\":null,\"featured-post\":true,\"author\":\"Generation Lab\",\"date\":\"2025-10-23T00:00:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"Generation Lab Raises $11M Seed Round as SystemAge™ Becomes World’s Fastest-Growing Longevity Diagnostic\",\"slug\":\"generation-lab-raises-11m-seed-round-as-systemage-tm-becomes-worlds-fastest-growing-longevity-diagnostic\"}},{\"id\":\"68eee95520719751fb734d6b\",\"cmsLocaleId\":\"66abe8ff91c980538e9fe16c\",\"lastPublished\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:36.811Z\",\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:36.811Z\",\"createdOn\":\"2025-10-15T00:22:45.247Z\",\"isArchived\":false,\"isDraft\":false,\"fieldData\":{\"post-body\":\"$28\",\"post-summary\":\"Explore in-depth reviews of the Thorne Gut Health Test. We break down what the results mean, the accuracy, and if this at-home test is worth the investment.\",\"main-image\":{\"fileId\":\"698d1ee3614d39f86145561b\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1ee3614d39f86145561b_68eee94f38f8888ad7ed08cc_Thorne%2520Gut%2520Health%2520Test%2520Reviews-%2520Is%2520the%2520Thorne%2520Test%2520Worth%2520It%253F.webp\",\"alt\":null},\"category\":null,\"featured-post\":false,\"author\":\"Alina Su\",\"date\":\"2025-10-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"Thorne Gut Health Test Reviews: Is the Thorne Test Worth It?\",\"slug\":\"thorne-gut-health-test-reviews\"}},{\"id\":\"68eee92a3e7b667645fdb727\",\"cmsLocaleId\":\"66abe8ff91c980538e9fe16c\",\"lastPublished\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:36.515Z\",\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:36.515Z\",\"createdOn\":\"2025-10-15T00:22:02.099Z\",\"isArchived\":false,\"isDraft\":false,\"fieldData\":{\"post-body\":\"$29\",\"post-summary\":\"Curious about your body's true age? Discover the top 4 methods to check your biological age, from telomere testing to epigenetic clocks. Find out how old you really are.\",\"main-image\":{\"fileId\":\"698d1edc8c875ef6ef9e2101\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1edc8c875ef6ef9e2101_68eee920fe66f884c71a7950_How%2520to%2520Check%2520Your%2520Biological%2520Age-%25204%2520Top%2520Methods.webp\",\"alt\":null},\"category\":null,\"featured-post\":false,\"author\":\"Alina Su\",\"date\":\"2025-10-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"How to Check Your Biological Age: 4 Top Methods\",\"slug\":\"how-to-check-biological-age\"}},{\"id\":\"68eee9094946dbd2cd3a7e06\",\"cmsLocaleId\":\"66abe8ff91c980538e9fe16c\",\"lastPublished\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:34.460Z\",\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:34.460Z\",\"createdOn\":\"2025-10-15T00:21:29.101Z\",\"isArchived\":false,\"isDraft\":false,\"fieldData\":{\"post-body\":\"$2a\",\"post-summary\":\"Compare Thorne and Viome's at-home gut health tests side-by-side. Our review covers accuracy, methodology, and cost to help you choose the best test for your needs.\",\"main-image\":{\"fileId\":\"698d1ee44c8beeffcee45617\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1ee44c8beeffcee45617_68eee90106172b549de57df3_Thorne%2520vs.%2520Viome-%2520Which%2520Gut%2520Health%2520Test%2520is%2520Best%253F.webp\",\"alt\":null},\"category\":null,\"featured-post\":false,\"author\":\"Alina Su\",\"date\":\"2025-10-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"Thorne vs. Viome: Which Gut Health Test is Best?\",\"slug\":\"thorne-vs-viome-gut-health-test\"}},{\"id\":\"68eee8c3de1c7d436e960e0b\",\"cmsLocaleId\":\"66abe8ff91c980538e9fe16c\",\"lastPublished\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:33.819Z\",\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-06-04T01:21:33.819Z\",\"createdOn\":\"2025-10-15T00:20:19.422Z\",\"isArchived\":false,\"isDraft\":false,\"fieldData\":{\"post-body\":\"$2b\",\"post-summary\":\"Discover seven scientifically proven strategies for age reversal. Learn how to slow down the aging process and live a longer, healthier life with these actionable tips.\",\"main-image\":{\"fileId\":\"698d1ed53f6350b7360bf4e9\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1ed53f6350b7360bf4e9_68eee8bd05d2aaca338d4e52_Age%2520Reversal-%25207%2520Science-Backed%2520Strategies.webp\",\"alt\":null},\"category\":null,\"featured-post\":false,\"author\":\"Alina Su\",\"date\":\"2025-10-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"Age Reversal: 7 Science-Backed Strategies\",\"slug\":\"age-reversal-strategies\"}}]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"23:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full py-[60px] lg:py-[100px]\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"linear-gradient(0deg, #241400 30.59%, #FBF6EE 60.84%, #FBF6EE 79.68%)\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2c\",null,{}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"25:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"lg:col-span-3 pt-[30vh] xl:pl-[60px] hidden lg:block\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full py-2 px-6 text-sm font-medium text-white cursor-pointer backdrop-blur-lg relative z-10 primary-button border border-white/20 transition-all duration-200 box-border flex justify-center items-center w-full h-[56px] no-underline\",\"style\":{},\"href\":\"/the-systemage-test\",\"children\":\"Find Your Biological Age →\"}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"17:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\"}]]\n13:null\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2d:I[80622,[],\"IconMark\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"15:{\"metadata\":[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Immune Age Test: Determine Your Immune System's Age\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Curious about your immune system's age? Learn how an Immune Age Test can determine its biological age and what the results mean for your health and longevity.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"Immune Age Test: Determine Your Immune System's Age\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Immune Age Test: Determine Your Immune System's Age\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Curious about your immune system's age? Learn how an Immune Age Test can determine its biological age and what the results mean for your health and longevity.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1ede92520c7f4ae58eb1_68eee8dfeb28d637f440a3d1_Immune%2520Age%2520Test-%2520Determine%2520Your%2520Immune%2520System%2527s%2520Age.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Immune Age Test: Determine Your Immune System's Age\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Curious about your immune system's age? Learn how an Immune Age Test can determine its biological age and what the results mean for your health and longevity.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66abe8ff91c980538e9fe18d/698d1ede92520c7f4ae58eb1_68eee8dfeb28d637f440a3d1_Immune%2520Age%2520Test-%2520Determine%2520Your%2520Immune%2520System%2527s%2520Age.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"10\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico\",\"type\":\"image/x-icon\",\"sizes\":\"48x48\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2d\",\"11\",{}]],\"error\":null,\"digest\":\"$undefined\"}\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1a:\"$1